  "intro": {
    "language": "en",
    "text": "John Francis Clauser (; born December 1, 1942) is an American theoretical and experimental physicist known for contributions to the foundations of quantum mechanics, in particular the Clauser–Horne–Shimony–Holt inequality.  Clauser was awarded the 2022 Nobel Prize in Physics, jointly with Alain Aspect and Anton Zeilinger \"for experiments with entangled photons, establishing the violation of Bell inequalities and pioneering quantum information science\". In 2023, he declared himself as a climate change denier.\n\n",
    "sourceId": "wikipedia-en",
    "usage": "Research excerpt; paraphrase and cross-check before publication."
  },
